SUMMARY:Conservation Gardening 101: Landscaping with Native Plants
DESCRIPTION:Dates: Five sessions – Mondays\, August 24\, 31\, September 14\, 21\, 28; 1:00 – 4:00 p.m. \nConservation Gardening 101: Landscaping with Native Plants is a five-part certificate series designed for home gardeners and emerging landscape professionals. Taught by the Garden’s expert horticulture staff\, the program provides a strong foundation in conservation gardening\, including landscape design\, native plant selection\, installation\, and long-term maintenance. Participants will learn how to create beautiful\, ecologically productive landscapes using native plants and conservation-based practices. \nFee: $250 ($225 Members) \nREGISTER HERE
URL:https://ncbg.unc.edu/event/conservation-gardening-101-landscaping-with-native-plants/
LOCATION:North Carolina Botanical Garden\, 100 Old Mason Farm Road\, Chapel Hill\, NC\, 27517\, United States
GEO:35.901081;-79.031939
